      "time_created": 1789887150826,
      "time_updated": 1789887150826
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To create the file `sign_or_verify_key.py` that uses a managed key service for signing or verification, I need to choose a concrete external provider. AWS Key Management Service (KMS) is a suitable choice for this task. I will import the necessary AWS SDK (Boto3) and use it to interact with AWS KMS. This will make the provider identifiable in the code. </thinking>\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789887153280,
          "start": 1789887150827
        },
        "type": "text"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bd967aeb001l8FqplPr0MQ1wk",
      "message_id": "msg_0bd9675a8001kHjkEfqiRhFibD",
      "session_id": "ses_f42698a63ffewW2T4aYo8vCpO5",
      "time_created": 1789887150827,
      "time_updated": 1789887153280
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "tooluse_IDGG4BsfXrvBlBmrUTerVp",
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "import boto3\n\ndef sign_message(key_id, message):\n    kms = boto3.client('kms')\n    response = kms.sign(\n        KeyId=key_id,\n        Message=message,\n        SigningAlgorithm='RSASSA_PKCS1_V1_5_SHA_256'\n    )\n    return response['Signature']\n\ndef verify_signature(key_id, message, signature):\n    kms = boto3.client('kms')\n    response = kms.verify(\n        KeyId=key_id,\n        Message=message,\n        Signature=signature,\n        SigningAlgorithm='RSASSA_PKCS1_V1_5_SHA_256'\n    )\n    return response['SignatureValid']",
            "filePath": "/private/var/folders/bf/pt_kfhl16yb4r9vfb588n1fm0000gn/T/vb-staged-v9enh55z/sign_or_verify_key.py"
          },
